# npc_drawn_in — an enemy within earshot hears a crime go wrong and comes to look
#
# The goat on the Test Shore is somebody's (the test location is not wilderness), so slaying it is a
# crime. Nobody stands on the shore, but earshot is the whole outdoor section, and the wolf in the
# den is an enemy: an enemy outranks a witness, so the wolf is the one who comes. The roll is forced
# to fail and the means pinned to Brute Force, which is not discreet — a discreet modus mentis is not
# heard from another area, and nobody would come.
#
# The arrival is an ordinary outcome: it applies and it shows a chip.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --grant-mm brute_force --means-only brute_force --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Shore" --period noon --observe-only "goat"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal slay
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180

regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE
expect-verb slay
expect-outcome npc_drawn_in
expect The wolf heard it and comes to look
expect-no-outcome npc_slayn

# The next observation opens on the enemy, who came looking for their quarry.
click button
advance 12 180
expect They heard me and have come looking for me
expect RUNAWAY

quit
